# node_modules is linked from the DSH installation during development
# (@deepseek-ai/schemastery); never committed.
node_modules/

# `lib/` is deliberately NOT ignored, and after the TypeScript migration it holds
# two different things:
#   - `lib/client.js` — hand-written SOURCE (the browser half; DSH loads it as a
#     classic script, `tsc` never compiles it). It must stay in the repo.
#   - the rest of `lib/` — build OUTPUT of `tsc -p tsconfig.json`, regenerated from
#     `src/` by `npm run build` (and by the `prepare` hook).
# Repo convention: `lib/` stays tracked (committed) so `file:` installs and the
# existing `test/*.mjs` paths keep working without running a build first.

